data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":2101,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0f24718771fe6fac016acb4c2649848196bcfd68f9cd903de0","call_id":"call_d1655c6120c44c768ab8e9b19439e229","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"test/ui.test.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"for (const archived of [false, true]) {\\n  test(`due date controls\",\"newText\":\"for (const archived of [false, true]) {\\n  test(`inclusive due ranges intersect filters (${archived ? 'archived' : 'active'})`, async () => {\\n    const app = new Node('main');\\n    const tasks = [\\n      { id: 1, title: 'Undated', completed: false, priority: 'High', dueDate: '' },\\n      { id: 2, title: 'Early', completed: false, priority: 'High', dueDate: '0001-01-01' },\\n      { id: 3, title: 'Leap', completed: false, priority: 'High', dueDate: '2000-02-29' },\\n      { id: 4, title: 'Done', completed: true, priority: 'High', dueDate: '2000-02-29' },\\n      { id: 5, title: 'Normal', completed: false, priority: 'Normal', dueDate: '2000-02-29' },\\n      { id: 6, title: 'Late', completed: false, priority: 'High', dueDate: '9999-12-31' },\\n    ];\\n    const original = structuredClone(tasks);\\n    const project = { id: 1, name: 'Ranges', archived, defaultTaskPriority: 'High' };\\n    let writes = 0;\\n    runInNewContext(source, {\\n      document: { querySelector: () => app, createElement: (tag) => new Node(tag) },\\n      location: { pathname: '/projects/1', assign() {} },\\n      async fetch(path, options) {\\n        let data;\\n        if (!options) data = path === '/api/projects/1' ? { ...project } : tasks.map((task) => ({ ...task }));\\n        else {\\n          writes++;\\n          const changes = JSON.parse(options.body);\\n          if (path === '/api/projects/1') {\\n            Object.assign(project, changes);\\n            data = { ...project };\\n          } else if (options.method === 'POST') {\\n            data = { id: 7, ...changes, priority: project.defaultTaskPriority, completed: false, dueDate: '' };\\n            tasks.push({ ...data });\\n          } else {\\n            const task = tasks.find((task) => path.endsWith(`/${task.id}`));\\n            Object.assign(task, changes);\\n            data = { ...task };\\n          }\\n        }\\n        return { ok: true, json: async () => data };\\n      },\\n    });\\n    await new Promise((resolve) => setImmediate(resolve));\\n    const filters = app.children.find((node) => node.className === 'task-filter');\\n    const completion = filters.children[1];\\n    const priority = filters.children[3];\\n    const range = app.children.find((node) => node.children[0]?.textContent === 'Due from');\\n    const from = range.children[1];\\n    const through = range.children[3];\\n    const titles = () => app.querySelector('ul').children.map((row) => row.children[1].textContent);\\n    const apply = async (start, end) => {\\n      from.value = start;\\n      through.value = end;\\n      await range.fire('submit');\\n    };\\n    assert.equal(from.value, '');\\n    assert.equal(through.value, '');\\n    assert.equal(from.type, 'text');\\n    assert.equal(through.type, 'text');\\n    assert.equal(range.children[0].htmlFor, from.id);\\n    assert.equal(range.children[2].textContent, 'Due through');\\n    assert.equal(range.children[2].htmlFor, through.id);\\n    assert.equal(range.children[4].textContent, 'Apply due range');\\n    assert.ok(!from.disabled && !through.disabled && !range.children[4].disabled);\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(), tasks.map((task) => task.title));\\n    await apply('', '0001-01-01');\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Early']);\\n    await apply('9999-12-31', '');\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Late']);\\n    await apply(' 2000-02-29 ', ' 2000-02-29 ');\\n    assert.equal(from.value, '2000-02-29');\\n    assert.equal(through.value, '2000-02-29');\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Leap', 'Done', 'Normal']);\\n    completion.value = 'Open';\\n    await completion.fire('change');\\n    priority.value = 'High';\\n    await priority.fire('change');\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Leap']);\\n    for (const invalid of ['1900-02-29', '0000-01-01', '2000-2-29', '2000-04-31', 'bad']) {\\n      await apply(invalid, '');\\n      assert.equal(app.querySelector('[role=\\\"alert\\\"]').textContent, 'Due range must use valid YYYY-MM-DD dates');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Leap']);\\n    }\\n    await apply('', '2001-02-29');\\n    assert.equal(app.querySelector('[role=\\\"alert\\\"]').textContent, 'Due range must use valid YYYY-MM-DD dates');\\n    await apply('2000-03-01', '2000-02-29');\\n    assert.equal(app.querySelector('[role=\\\"alert\\\"]').textContent, 'Due from must not be after Due through');\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Leap']);\\n    // Draft (including invalid) boundaries do not replace the applied range.\\n    priority.value = 'All';\\n    await priority.fire('change');\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Leap', 'Normal']);\\n    assert.equal(completion.value, 'Open');\\n    assert.equal(writes, 0);\\n    assert.deepEqual(tasks, original);\\n    if (!archived) {\\n      priority.value = 'High';\\n      await priority.fire('change');\\n      const row = () => app.querySelector('ul').children[0];\\n      const rename = row().children[2];\\n      rename.children[1].value = 'Renamed';\\n      await rename.fire('submit');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Renamed']);\\n      const renameProject = app.children.find((node) => node.children[0]?.textContent === 'New project name');\\n      renameProject.children[1].value = 'New name';\\n      await renameProject.fire('submit');\\n      const defaults = app.children.find((node) => node.children[0]?.textContent === 'Default task priority');\\n      defaults.children[1].value = 'Low';\\n      await defaults.children[1].fire('change');\\n      const create = app.children.find((node) => node.children[0]?.textContent === 'Task title');\\n      create.children[1].value = 'New undated';\\n      await create.fire('submit');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Renamed']);\\n      const date = row().children[5];\\n      date.children[1].value = '2000-03-01';\\n      await date.fire('submit');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), []);\\n      await apply('2000-03-01', '2000-03-01');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Renamed']);\\n      const taskPriority = row().children[4];\\n      taskPriority.value = 'Low';\\n      await taskPriority.fire('change');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), []);\\n      priority.value = 'Low';\\n      await priority.fire('change');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Renamed']);\\n      const checkbox = row().children[0];\\n      checkbox.checked = true;\\n      await checkbox.fire('change');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), []);\\n      completion.value = 'Completed';\\n      await completion.fire('change');\\n      assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Renamed']);\\n      assert.equal(priority.value, 'Low');\\n      assert.equal(from.value, '2000-03-01');\\n      assert.equal(through.value, '2000-03-01');\\n    }\\n    await apply('  ', '\\\\t');\\n    completion.value = 'All';\\n    await completion.fire('change');\\n    priority.value = 'All';\\n    await priority.fire('change');\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(), tasks.map((task) => task.title));\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfor (const archived of [false, true]) {\\n  test(`due date controls\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":2102,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_0f24718771fe6fac016acb4c2116dc8196bc335e8d5f1b80d0","object":"response","created_at":1791708193,"completed_at":1791708235,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nPrioritize maintainability and clean code throughout the project. Before editing, understand the current design and identify the smallest coherent change that meets the requirements. Keep responsibilities clear, modules cohesive, and dependencies explicit. Use descriptive names, consistent conventions, and simple interfaces. Separate business rules from presentation, persistence, and external integrations where that makes future changes easier.\n\nPrefer straightforward implementations over speculative abstractions. Remove meaningful duplication without coupling unrelated concerns. Keep functions and modules focused; avoid hidden state and surprising side effects. Handle invalid inputs, errors, and resource cleanup explicitly. Preserve compatibility and data integrity when changing persistence or interfaces.\n\nAdd and maintain useful automated tests for business rules, important boundaries, and regressions. Use the appropriate formatter, static analysis, and type checks for the stack. Run relevant checks and address failures before submission. Refactor touched areas when doing so makes the current change and later development easier, while preserving behavior and keeping the work reviewable.\n\nKeep dependencies intentional, configuration explicit, and setup reproducible. Document non-obvious decisions, public contracts, and operational requirements. Remove dead code and stale documentation. Keep commits coherent and describe the reason for each change. Revisit earlier design decisions as requirements grow. Do not pad the codebase, build speculative frameworks, or optimize for line count.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0f24718771fe6fac016acb4c2343688196aa1e9ea056086db5","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Considering test strategies**\n\nI'm thinking about needing new tests to append extensively via bash. It seems like I can't append directly, so I have to create a new file. That means I need to focus on unique or separate test files to avoid duplication. I'll be careful to insert things before any existing tests. Additionally, I want to consider an active/archive loop for testing ranges, and how I might manage dynamic edits with tasks."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqy0wmnFE7PnbuFNe7xq_nD5DfMFKxurI19uAdmPcLG_IPmJR--cXOUzEazVpUE5aR4Od4eIOeIDvPKm056X6D4sV8upoewawDP3nnPie6_CvOQ5PJfl-1zMD8Pl5YldFDAkJShc2rFVEZwy3W7nfdP2gkiOkmdudYSDK5gRANijoB-Kxqmwyf8LfViybw1qfCOCbWRhrtAArYwfFMR1hhsGJlnv296fl-PTFjyh7tqBsc5K9zNpImW0xn4nP1yedKzVBKbCiExzrFFxWrfppNi8VEw91l-sLGMQcvwAuL80t0QP1SBvaeGpX67BGLg-rFZ4sxnS7V-SQq7h0OR3VHa8EH6fFBT3CpYIPKyQspMzIf0Db4JUZdwX7NL53GeCcJebfV7Qk8H0YXEeyxo21039-f27CzEQrMqFsNsQZ4BCC8Mxu5R63Gd5w4Qu8kBiBupaStWsc3gPRFNNeY6ierIRpQnlm8IIs_JoCaiJ6t7pkCZKKmAjemGiB6